# Rendered reels: regenerate with site/scripts/gen-reel.mjs
*.mp4
.reel-frames/
# Exception: unlisted video pages under /v/<random>/ serve a real file from
# GitHub Pages, so their source has to be committed. Without this negation
# the blanket *.mp4 above drops the video from the commit silently and the
# page deploys with a player that has nothing behind it.
# Both paths are required. site/public/ is the source, and v/ is where the
# deploy step copies it at the repo root; that copy is committed by the
# workflow's own `git add -A`, which obeys this file too. Exempting only the
# source is how the first deploy shipped a page whose video 404'd.
!site/public/v/**/*.mp4
!v/**/*.mp4

# API keys. This repo is public: nothing resembling a secret goes in it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.key
.dev.vars
